fix(email-ingest): whitelist internal tick route in middleware

Edge middleware was redirecting POST /api/internal/email-ingest/tick to
/login because the route is under /api but isn't in the PUBLIC_PATHS
list. Add it. The route handler still authenticates via constant-time
compare against INGEST_TICK_SECRET; the 127.0.0.1 bind + UFW keep the
endpoint off the public internet.

Verified locally: pnpm run build clean, route appears under "Routes
(app)" without warnings.
